In the evening Nina knocks on my door.
She comes in, and we talk together.
"Are you happy with your new job?" Nina asks.
"Yes, I am very happy," I answer.
"Tomorrow morning I have time off," I explain.
"I am going to the municipality."
"I need to get my CPR number."
Nina nods and gives me a good tip.
"You need a Danish phone number," she says.
"It is a good idea to get it first."
"You need the number for the forms."
"That is a good tip," I say happily.
"Then I will buy a SIM card tomorrow."
Now I have a good plan for tomorrow.
